    "decisionSummary": "Jinn 0.0.17 answers the second half of an owner report filed against the live tenant on 2026-08-22. With a Domain Template Grain and a mini-git pearl both attached and healthy the assistant said it had no way to enumerate its connections; it was right, because the chat catalog is assembled from GrainContext-speaking pearls and a pearl contributes tool entries but never a fact about itself, while a DTG speaks no GrainContext at all. pearls.list reads the registry instead, and reports granted authority as a sentence rather than an enum so the assistant repeats a fact instead of translating one. It never returns the sturdyref token. The same line's 0.0.16 built the write-authority path the first half of that report needed. The commit message on this exact dev-publish tip records both, with the mutations run against every guard. Main remains the reviewed baseline; the dev-publish head is the release authority, as for every other row in this catalog.",
